.newsect Cheating!
.!
I'd only be able to get your attention faster if I offered free
Calastoga Mineral Water :-).
Wanna delve deep into the guts of an application
and pull out something that is hidden in a dark corner?
Come a little closer and I shall depart a few tibits of knowledge
before tomorrow when I must travel again.
But tonight my stories can be had for an pint of ale.
.!
.!
.sect 1 1 Extracting Instance Variables
  Although objects are supposed to be complete and inaccessible from
outside the methods code, you can access the variables if you
really need to.
From inside a class you can reference any superclasses' instance
variables using "self->" in front of the reference.
.!
.opencode

- (int) capacity
{
    /* reach into another class and read its mind! */
    struct { @defs(IdArray) }   *id_ptr;

    id_ptr = (void *) self->contents;    /* Grab pointer to array obj */
    printf( "its capacity=%d\n", id_ptr->capacity );

    return( [id_ptr capacity] );
}

.endcode
.figname Referencing Instance Variables


.!
.endsect
